      "evidence": "template/scripts/publication_queue.py restore_gates calls _transition(root, repo, number, candidate[\"state\"], candidate[\"head\"], task_identity=..., inherit_identity=False, gates=gates). In _transition, next_job is taken from previous.get(\"next_job\") and previous is {} when the head has no record; red_gate=None is also passed. The state is therefore preserved but its job and red-gate context may not be.",
      "id": "restore-gates-drops-next-job-and-red-gate",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "restore-gates republishes the candidate's state through _transition without passing the derived candidate's next_job or red_gate. When no exact-head record exists (for example a review-pending candidate derived from a validated-push receipt, or blocked-retryable), the new record can lose the pending job or red gate even though the design says the state is kept."
    }
